A statement that lost its `;` right before a line-leading :IF. The
continuation reading applies only when the word after the colon is not a
keyword, so :IF still lexes as a keyword; unexpected_token reports it,
mentioning the previous statement may be missing its `;`. The :IF block
must still pair with its :ENDIF (diag.unexpected_token, diag.unknown_keyword
lexer guard).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE BumpVersion;
	:PARAMETERS nVersion;
	nVersion := nVersion + 1
	:IF nVersion > 99;
		nVersion := 1;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nVersion;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE BumpVersion;
	:PARAMETERS nVersion;
	nVersion := nVersion + 1;
	:IF nVersion > 99;
		nVersion := 1;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nVersion;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:2-4:5 error unexpected_token: Unexpected keyword ':IF' - expected an operator or ';' (is the previous statement missing its ';'?)
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:2-4:5 error unexpected_token: Unexpected keyword ':IF' - expected an operator or ';' (is the previous statement missing its ';'?)
